{"block_id": "36", "heading": null, "source": "འོན་ཀྱང་འཆི་བདག་ཁར་ཕྱོགས་པའི། །\nསྲོག་གི་རྒྱུན་ནི་མ་ནུབ་པར། །\nཁྱོད་ལ་ཅུང་ཟད་ཡིད་ཆེས་པ། །\nདེ་ཡང་སྐལ་བ་བཟང་སྙམ་བགྱིད། །", "translation": "Nevertheless, before the stream of life heading toward the jaws of the Lord of Death has ceased,\nThat I have gained even a slight conviction in You—\nThis too, I consider to be good fortune.", "target_language": "english", "focus": "tibetan", "style_instruction": "Translate this Tibetan verse of praise line by line: render each Tibetan line as one line of the target language, in the same order, and keep the same number of lines as the source. Devotional but clear register. Keep mantra syllables and proper names in transliteration rather than translating them. Do not add commentary, notes, or explanation.", "context": "Work: བློ་སྦྱོང་ཚིག་བརྒྱད་མ། (author: གླང་རི་ཐང་པ།). A canonical Tibetan text; the blocks below are being translated one at a time, in order.\n\nPreceding blocks of this same document and their translations — match this terminology, register and line shape:\n\n[33] source:\nཨེ་མའོ་མཁས་པས་འདི་གཉིས་ཀྱི། །\nཁྱད་པར་ཁོང་དུ་ཆུད་གྱུར་པ། །\nདེ་ཚེ་རྐང་གི་ཁོང་ནས་ནི། །\nཁྱོད་ལ་ཅི་ཕྱིར་གུས་མི་འགྱུར། །\n[33] translation already produced for this document:\nHow wonderful! When a wise person\nHas thoroughly understood the difference between these two,\nThen, from the very marrow of their bones,\nWhy would they not feel devotion to You?\n\n[34] source:\nཁྱོད་གསུང་དུ་མ་ཅི་ཞིག་སྨོས། །\nཆ་ཤས་རེ་ཡི་དོན་ཙམ་ལའང་། །\nའོལ་སྤྱི་ཙམ་གྱི་ངེས་རྙེད་པ། །\nདེ་ལའང་མཆོག་གི་བདེ་བ་སྟེར། །\n[34] translation already produced for this document:\nWhat need is there to speak of Your many teachings?\nEven regarding the meaning of just a fraction of them,\nGaining certainty, even if only in a general way,\nBestows supreme happiness.\n\n[35] source:\nཀྱི་ཧུད་བདག་བློ་རྨོངས་པས་བཅོམ། །\nའདི་འདྲའི་ཡོན་ཏན་ཕུང་པོ་ལ། །\nརིང་ནས་སྐྱབས་སུ་སོང་གྱུར་ཀྱང་། །\nཡོན་ཏན་ཆ་ཙམ་མ་འཚལ་ཏོ། །\n[35] translation already produced for this document:\nAlas! My mind is conquered by delusion;\nAlthough I have long taken refuge in such a mass of excellence,\nI have not understood even a fraction of Your qualities.", "endpoint": "https://dharmamitra.org/api-search/cat-translate/v1/translate", "batch_size": 5, "batch_block_ids": ["36", "37", "38", "39", "40"], "batch_fallback": false, "elapsed_s": 4.97, "ts": "2026-08-27T23:06:26"}
