5] source:\nཕན་མཛད་དེ་ཡི་བསྟན་པའང་སྲིད་པའི་མཐར། །\nངན་རྟོག་རླུང་གིས་རྣམ་པར་མི་གཡོ་ཞིང་། །\nབསྟན་པའི་ངང་ཚུལ་ཤེས་ནས་སྟོན་པ་ལ། །\nཡིད་ཆེས་རྙེད་པས་རྟག་ཏུ་གང་བར་ཤོག །\n[55] translation already produced for this document:\nMay the teachings of that Benefactor, until the end of existence,\nNot be shaken by the winds of false conceptual thoughts,\nAnd having known the nature of the teachings, may I always be filled\nWith the conviction found in the Teacher.", "endpoint": "https://dharmamitra.org/api-search/cat-translate/v1/translate", "batch_size": 3, "batch_block_ids": ["56", "57", "58"], "batch_fallback": false, "elapsed_s": 1.69, "ts": "2026-08-27T23:06:50"}
{"block_id": "35", "heading": null, "source": "ཀྱི་ཧུད་བདག་བློ་རྨོངས་པས་བཅོམ། །\nའདི་འདྲའི་ཡོན་ཏན་ཕུང་པོ་ལ། །\nརིང་ནས་སྐྱབས་སུ་སོང་གྱུར་ཀྱང་། །\nཡོན་ཏན་ཆ་ཙམ་མ་འཚལ་ཏོ། །", "translation": "Alas! My mind has been conquered by delusion;\nThough I have long taken refuge in such a mass of excellence,\nAnd have long since gone for refuge,\nI have not understood even a fraction of your qualities.", "target_language": "english", "focus": "tibetan", "style_instruction": "Translate this Tibetan verse of praise line by line: render each Tibetan line as one line of the target language, in the same order, and keep the same number of lines as the source. Devotional but clear register. Keep mantra syllables and proper names in transliteration rather than translating them. Do not add commentary, notes, or explanation.\n\nLINE-BY-LINE (strict): the source has 4 numbered lines, each prefixed '1| ', '2| ' and so on. Output exactly 4 lines carrying the SAME prefixes. Line N of your output must translate line N of the source and nothing else: do not move content between lines, and do not merge or split lines. Output only the numbered lines -- no heading, no blank lines, no commentary.", "context": "Work: བློ་སྦྱོང་ཚིག་བརྒྱད་མ། (author: གླང་རི་ཐང་པ།). A canonical Tibetan text; the blocks below are being translated one at a time, in order.\n\nPreceding blocks of this same document and their translations — match this terminology, register and line shape:\n\n[56] source:\nབརྟེན་ནས་འབྱུང་བའི་དེ་ཉིད་གསལ་མཛད་པ། །\nཐུབ་པའི་ལུགས་བཟང་སྐྱེ་བ་ཐམས་ཅད་དུ། །\nལུས་དང་སྲོག་ཀྱང་བཏང་ནས་འཛིན་པ་ལ། །\nསྐད་ཅིག་ཙམ་ཡང་ལྷོད་པར་མ་གྱུར་ཅིག །\n[56] translation already produced for this document:\nMay I clarify the reality of dependent arising,\nAnd in all my lives, within the excellent tradition of the Sage,\nHold it fast, having surrendered even my body and life,\nWithout becoming lax for even a single moment.\n\n[57] source:\nའདྲེན་པ་མཆོག་དེས་དཀའ་བ་དཔག་མེད་ཀྱིས། །ྃ\nནན་ཏན་སྙིང་པོར་མཛད་ནས་བསྒྲུབས་པ་འདི། །ྃ\nཐབས་གང་